WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.560
Child speech recognition now retains adult performance through bilingual adaptation and weight merging. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 197. Researchers released a study on child ASR adaptation that preserves adult performance across Arabic and English. They compared full fine-tuning, Laura and post-hoc weight space merging on encoder decoder, encoder CTC and audio LLM systems.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.440
Bilingual adaptation proved more stable than language-specific approaches.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.140
LERP merging favored adult retention while TIES recovered stronger child gains.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.520
Direct bilingual fine-tuning remained strongest in raw word error rate for the encoder decoder model.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.400
The work quantifies the adaptation retention trade-off with retention index,

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:56.700
context, child adaptation gain, and adaptation recovery metrics on MyST, MGB2, and Libre

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.580
speech benchmarks.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.620
Code and models are available at the linked GitHub repository.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.820
In Model Updates, Code AR adds a training-free refinement pass to mask diffusion language

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:08.300
models.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.100
It detects confidence drift in committed tokens via K partition probing.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.640
The method remasks and regenerates only tokens the model no longer endorses after

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.000
or denser context arrives.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:26.140
Code AR improved average accuracy across two backbones for reasoning and coding tasks

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.940
and three base samplers.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.980
It used fewer forward passes than prior remasking approaches.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.220
A gated cross-attention framework integrates emotionally rewritten news with LLM-generated

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.280
explanations from original articles.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.200
Experiments on PoliteFact, GossipCop, and LUN showed notable gains under multiple

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:52.480
emotional conditions on two of the three datasets. The approach reduces mismatches caused by emotional

00:01:52.480 --> 00:02:01.340
reframing while maintaining competitive performance on the third dataset. A large scale study of 103,939

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:08.640
graded replies across eight LLMs and two reasoning configurations found that task verification cost and

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.160
hardware coverage dominate sickofancy rates.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.000
Anchored facts saw only 1.3% concessions.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.100
Personal choices were endorsed in 77% of conversations.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.180
Maximum reasoning eliminated concessions

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.560
on deep puzzles for both models tested.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.680
LRCC trains lightweight routers per transformer block

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.160
to select among nested lower-ank paths

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.720
on a token-dependent basis.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:37.200
On LAMA and Quinn models, it delivered a 7.6%

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:43.800
point gain in average downstream accuracy over static low-rank compression at matched active parameter

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:52.100
budget. At batch size 1 decoding latency, it improved both perplexity and accuracy on LAMMA 3.21B

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:59.100
without specialized kernels. 3.8.7 million parameter Chinese BERT models were trained from scratch

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.300
under identical conditions. MLM won three of five intrinsic dimensions.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:11.080
WWM achieved 39.5% better perplexity and higher MLM hit rate.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.320
MacBert, under a 222 entries synonym dictionary,

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:20.740
produced 47.23 perplexity, 22 times higher than MLM.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:26.080
Care provides finite sample guarantees that acceleration-induced failure risk

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.740
stays below a user-specified budget.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:32.600
On four Libero-sweets with open VLA-OFT,

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.820
it's certified 9.0 to 10.8 times speed-ups.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:44.080
It guarantees at 95% that at least 85.8% of reference-solved episodes are preserved.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:51.160
Tool Eraser generates validated multi-turn trajectories across six domains and 55 personas.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:58.300
It produced 5.6K conversations with approximately 66% containing failure-prone scenarios.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:03.880
Models trained on the resulting benchmark improved end-to-end agentic accuracy on

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:09.040
Towsquared Bench and Ace Bench. A two-stage pipeline first detects cognitive

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:14.120
components, then generates a line dialogue using knowledge distillation, preference

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:19.860
optimization, and attention-guided reward shaping. Cognitively informed fine-tuning

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:25.540
produce substantial gains in cognitive realization over generic instruction tuned and mental

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.100
health domain SLMs.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:34.580
SUDO dialect speech synthesized from LLM generated dialect text via standard language TTS improved

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:38.180
dialect to English translation scores for Japanese and German.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:46.720
Intermediate standard text prediction further boosted Japanese to 28.26 and Chinese to 16.37.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:53.240
Online QAT performs on-policy distillation on student-generated responses after

00:04:53.240 --> 00:05:03.560
blockwise QAT initialization. On QAN 3.1.7B it reached 57.28 average at W3A16 and

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:12.700
32.52 at W2A16. It outperformed reasoning QAT by 2.90 and 0.44 points

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:20.400
respectively. SK-bench supplies 30 data sets across 10 skill categories with 11 newly introduced

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:26.880
or packaged resources. The best open model trailed proprietary API is by 12.6 points.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:34.760
Continued pre-training on Quinn 314b lowered overall score by 13.9 points before instruction

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:41.080
repair recovered three quarters of the loss. The adversarial surface form robustness data set contains

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.960
between 2,100 prompts across seven surface-form families.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.060
Emoji and Invisible Unicode Variations

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:53.600
produced 20.27% and 17.20% harmful compliance

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.520
against a 22.87% baseline.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.460
LeetSpeak and encoded wrappers raised comprehension failure

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:05.700
to 36.47% and 65.60%.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.180
Use-based projects token states on to an orthogonal basis

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.260
derived from semantic anchors for doubt and certainty.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.960
The resulting confidence score outperformed established baselines under both

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.900
standard and length-controlled evaluation. It transferred more reliably than

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.960
supervised estimators without requiring correctness labels or repeated

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.940
generations. Goldsmith iteratively revises annotation

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:33.780
definitions by running candidate definitions on a small gold set.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:41.020
It outperformed direct rewriting, OPRO, APE, and prompt breeder under matched protocols.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:46.640
Mean difference activation steering on Moshe's residual stream decodes four emotions

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.480
linearly, yet achieves only partial and uneven control.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:56.620
Happy, angry, and surprise share one direction while sad remains distinctly steerable.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.220
The shared component cannot be projected away uniformly.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:05.400
The approach requires only a few vector additions per frame with low retraining.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:12.780
Performance varies because the geometry of the residual stream groups three emotions together limiting independent control.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.320
When the target emotion lies along the shared direction, steering succeeds.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.080
When it requires an orthogonal offset, success drops.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:28.700
Teams needing reliable affect control should measure per emotion's durability on their specific model before deployment.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:34.480
Try the KODR refinement pass on your mask diffusion language model sampling pipeline

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:39.340
for reasoning or coding tasks to recover accuracy with modest overhead.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:45.620
Experiment with LRCC routers on LAMA 3.21B or KWEN models

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:49.560
when you need token dependent compute allocation without custom kernels.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.640
Evaluate SK bench on your Slovak language applications

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:56.840
to measure native performance versus translated baselines

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.540
before scaling pre-training.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:03.180
Test care-certified acceleration on open VLA OFT

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:07.040
or similar VLA models when you require guaranteed failure

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.820
bounds below a chosen budget.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.400
Continued releases of controlled comparison studies

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.540
on tiny-scale pre-training strategies

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.340
are expected in the coming weeks.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.580
Additional benchmarks for under-resource languages

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.020
and dialect robustness are anticipated

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:28.040
from multiple labs. Further work on certified acceleration and on-policy distillation for

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:33.960
low-bit models is likely to appear soon. Pop the hood on emotion steering in full duplex

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:38.980
speech models and the picture changes from uniform control to geometry-limited results.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.960
Mean difference activation steering works by adding a few factors per frame to Moshe's residual

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:51.400
stream. Four emotions decode linearly from that stream. Three of them collapse onto one shared

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:57.480
direction. Sad stays orthogonal and therefore steerable on its own. The shared direction

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:02.180
cannot be subtracted equally from all four emotions without distorting the distinct one.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:07.640
Steering therefore succeeds when the target emotion aligns with the shared vector and

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:12.800
fails when it needs an independent offset. The practical limit appears at the point where

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:18.540
three emotions share geometry while the fourth does not. Measure steerability per emotion

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:22.420
on the target model rather than assuming uniform results across the set.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:29.420
Before we go, watch for new certified acceleration results on additional VLA suites expected in

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.420
the next several days.

